  "observation_conventions": "Native pixels. June is the 2144 by 1424 Fayhoo photograph; the December renderings are 840 by 560. Occluded upper openings are bounded by the winter views. Original photographs are not included.",
  "known_limits": "Window placements and apron faces are measured from the images. Rail bar depths, repeating steel bar sections, the projection of the west wall and individual glass depths are estimates. The west station has a weak baseline to the west lower lights; its independent placement fit had 5–19 pixel errors and inconsistent depth, so its apparent blind middle infill and two surviving balconies constrain the counts only. The middle three-window bay has a distinct sill on each front facet; no window is placed through the west blind panel beneath the air conditioner.",
